      "pm_ruling_2026-11-03": "Keep Laporta thresholds as the energies of record because the potential curve also produced the cross sections, preserving detailed-balance consistency. The three-term Dunham expression is a low-v spectroscopy fit; smooth high-v divergence is attributed to truncation extrapolation, not a Laporta data error. The PM stated agreement <=0.001 eV through v=21; the reproduced v=21 difference is 0.00176014667 eV, as disclosed in recomputed_gate_note.",
      "recomputed_gate_note": "The committed per-level calculation gives |dE|=0.00176014667 eV at v=21, so the <=0.001 eV statement is numerically satisfied only through v=20. The Laporta source-of-record ruling remains accepted; the independent stop threshold was 0.005 eV, first exceeded at v=24."
